WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.092
Budget Rules is a feature in Campaign Manager that helps you manage and optimize your budget.

00:00:08.092 --> 00:00:15.679
It can automatically increase your budget during a specific timeframe, or when your campaign hits

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:17.702
a certain performance target.

00:00:17.702 --> 00:00:26.300
You can use budget rules to help you keep top performing campaigns running, to prevent budget being

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.323
spent on underperforming campaigns.

00:00:28.323 --> 00:00:29.840
To reduce time,

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:35.680
spent monitoring and manually adjusting your campaigns and optimize your budget for key events

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.137
with personalized recommendations.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:40.537
There are two types of budget rules.

00:00:40.537 --> 00:00:42.480
Scheduled-based rules allow

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:49.280
you to set budgets in advance for special events, such as Prime Day or Halloween or during a date

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.859
range of your choice.

00:00:50.859 --> 00:00:55.200
For example, during an important shopping event such as Black Friday,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:01.120
you can set your budget to increase by 50% to help make the most of the anticipated increase in

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:01.526
shoppers.

00:01:01.526 --> 00:01:06.800
Performance-based rules will increase your campaign budget when your campaign meets a

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:12.217
certain performance threshold, such as ROAS, click-through rate or conversion rate.

00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:13.120
For example,

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:17.840
if you want your budget to increase when your campaign is performing well, you could set your

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.440
budget to increase by 20% when your ROAS hits 5.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.320
Make sure to apply budget rules during your

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.685
next important event to help make the most of your campaign.

00:01:27.685 --> 00:01:29.520
Check out our follow-on video

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:35.440
to find out how to set up a budget rule.
